node_modules/

# Publish artifacts. `npm pack` drops amber-console-<version>.tgz in the repo
# root — 180kb of the repo, committed back into the repo.
*.tgz
*.log

# NEVER COMMIT THIS. `npm login` and `npm token` can write an auth token into a
# project-local .npmrc, and committing one publishes a credential that can push
# to this package. Ignored by default; if you ever need a checked-in .npmrc for
# registry config, `git add -f .npmrc` after checking there is no token in it.
.npmrc
.env
.env.*

# Visual-regression run output — written only for a capture that FAILED, so it
# can be eyeballed against its baseline. Throwaway; the next run rewrites it.
test/visual/*.actual.png

# scripts/make-assets.mjs unlinks this; it only survives a crashed run.
docs/.make-assets.tmp.html

# Local tool state, machine-specific
.claude/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTHING HERE IGNORES test/visual/baselines/, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
#
# It briefly did. 157 hand-listed filenames — the same 44 files enumerated
# three times over — sat here to keep 11.6MB of PNGs out of the repository,
# while the comment above test/visual/*.actual.png claimed baselines/ was
# committed. Both could not be true, and the way it resolved was silent: the
# 30 baselines already tracked stayed tracked, because an ignore does not
# untrack, and the 14 for server.html and terminal.html — the two newest demo
# pages — were never committed at all. Two of the four demos had no visual
# coverage in the repo and the suite could not tell anyone, because a file
# that is ignored is not reported as missing.
#
# A baseline IS the test. Ignoring it does not save the repository from the
# bytes, it only saves them from being reviewed, and it costs the one thing
# the suite exists for: a fresh clone that can say whether the pages still
# render the way they did. The full set is committed as of 2.0, and adding a
# thirteenth page means committing its baselines with it.

